WEBVTT

1
00:00:02,208 --> 00:00:04,208
[birds chirping]

2
00:00:07,208 --> 00:00:10,500
Oh, Pascal, it would've been so great
to have one of these

3
00:00:10,583 --> 00:00:12,917
when I was locked up in that tower.
[chuckling]

4
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:16,500
-Oh, so cute! Aw.
-[cooing]

5
00:00:16,583 --> 00:00:19,958
Whoa, that doesn't look good.
[chuckles nervously]

6
00:00:20,042 --> 00:00:25,000
Dark, ominous clouds usually make me think
something villainous is afoot.

7
00:00:25,083 --> 00:00:27,833
Oh! It's just a little bit of rain.

8
00:00:27,917 --> 00:00:30,833
Aw, but the bunnies are all getting wet.

9
00:00:30,917 --> 00:00:32,500
And the birds.

10
00:00:32,583 --> 00:00:35,292
[gasps] And that itty-bitty ant.

11
00:00:35,375 --> 00:00:39,167
Pascal, all these poor little critters
are out there in the rain.

12
00:00:39,250 --> 00:00:40,917
[thunder rumbling]

13
00:00:41,792 --> 00:00:44,042
[mumbles indistinctly]

14
00:00:44,125 --> 00:00:49,417
[sighs] I know the ocean is my friend,
but I do like being nice and dry inside.

15
00:00:49,500 --> 00:00:53,625
I used to want to escape the palace,
but not on a day like this.

16
00:00:53,708 --> 00:00:54,875
[thunder crashes]

17
00:00:54,958 --> 00:00:57,417
[sighs] I think it's perfect weather
for a quiet day--

18
00:00:57,500 --> 00:00:58,875
[caws loudly]

19
00:00:58,958 --> 00:01:01,417
-Inside.
-Sorry, he's--

20
00:01:01,500 --> 00:01:03,167
-[Heihei caws]
-Heihei.

21
00:01:03,250 --> 00:01:05,792
-[all chuckling]
-Technically, under the sea,

22
00:01:05,875 --> 00:01:08,042
every day is a rainy one.

23
00:01:08,125 --> 00:01:09,958
Such a downpour!

24
00:01:10,042 --> 00:01:13,000
I hope the animals
can stay warm and dry out there.

25
00:01:13,083 --> 00:01:14,875
It feels like I should be helping them.

26
00:01:14,958 --> 00:01:16,208
Don't feel too bad.

27
00:01:16,292 --> 00:01:19,583
Wild animals don't mind a passing storm.
They'll make the most of the day.

28
00:01:19,667 --> 00:01:20,750
And so will we.

29
00:01:20,833 --> 00:01:24,833
I, for one, am happy to relax
and enjoy a cozy afternoon indoors.

30
00:01:24,917 --> 00:01:26,333
[chuckles]

31
00:01:26,417 --> 00:01:29,417
Some relax with card games,

32
00:01:29,500 --> 00:01:32,292
others relax with chaos!

33
00:01:32,375 --> 00:01:36,583
[chuckles] Let's see how relaxing this is.

34
00:01:36,667 --> 00:01:38,792
-[thunder crashes]
-[Cheshire Cat chuckles]

35
00:01:41,750 --> 00:01:42,833
Your turn, Ariel.

36
00:01:43,792 --> 00:01:45,750
[gasps] Two geese.

37
00:01:45,833 --> 00:01:48,250
-Go fish!
-No, um...

38
00:01:48,333 --> 00:01:50,750
Oh! [chuckles] Don't mind us, dearies.

39
00:01:50,833 --> 00:01:52,667
Just looking for the bathtub!

40
00:01:52,750 --> 00:01:55,583
-[geese laughing]
-Uh, it's that way.

41
00:01:55,667 --> 00:01:58,458
-[both] Thank you!
-These accommodations are simply divine.

42
00:01:58,542 --> 00:01:59,833
So divine.

43
00:01:59,917 --> 00:02:02,125
Uh, we all saw that, right?

44
00:02:02,208 --> 00:02:06,292
The only special ingredient
I put in the tea was love, I promise.

45
00:02:06,375 --> 00:02:07,542
What is going on?

46
00:02:07,625 --> 00:02:09,292
-Huh?
-Whoa.

47
00:02:09,375 --> 00:02:11,667
[mumbling indistinctly, groans]

48
00:02:11,750 --> 00:02:13,125
[piano playing]

49
00:02:13,208 --> 00:02:14,417
[Heihei screeches]

50
00:02:14,500 --> 00:02:16,208
[chirps]

51
00:02:16,292 --> 00:02:18,000
Where are these animals coming from?

52
00:02:18,083 --> 00:02:20,458
Huh. Maybe they did mind the storm.

53
00:02:20,542 --> 00:02:23,000
There must be a window or door
open somewhere.

54
00:02:23,083 --> 00:02:25,542
Let's split up and investigate.

55
00:02:25,625 --> 00:02:27,083
[all grunt]

56
00:02:28,917 --> 00:02:34,042
Cozy afternoon, indeed! [chuckles]

57
00:02:36,042 --> 00:02:37,042
[thunder crashes]

58
00:02:38,000 --> 00:02:39,125
[gasps, grunts]

59
00:02:39,208 --> 00:02:43,375
How do these bunnies keep multiplying?
Hey! Stop that.

60
00:02:43,458 --> 00:02:46,292
-[objects clattering]
-[gasps]

61
00:02:47,667 --> 00:02:48,750
[grunts]

62
00:02:50,708 --> 00:02:51,792
[gasps]

63
00:02:51,875 --> 00:02:53,625
-[growls]
-Oh, would you like a--

64
00:02:54,250 --> 00:02:55,458
-Pie? [chuckles nervously]
-[grunts]

65
00:02:57,792 --> 00:03:00,250
-I don't hear anything, do you?
-[trills]

66
00:03:02,542 --> 00:03:03,625
-[birds chirping]
-[gasps] Ooh!

67
00:03:03,708 --> 00:03:05,000
[chuckles]

68
00:03:05,083 --> 00:03:06,167
Whoa! [chuckles]

69
00:03:07,333 --> 00:03:10,042
-[birds screeching]
-Whoa! [screams, grunts]

70
00:03:15,375 --> 00:03:18,583
The dining room's secure. [gasps] Huh.

71
00:03:18,667 --> 00:03:20,208
[monkeys screeching]

72
00:03:21,458 --> 00:03:25,792
I take that back.
The dining room is definitely not secure.

73
00:03:25,875 --> 00:03:26,875
[grunts]

74
00:03:29,750 --> 00:03:31,375
-[Heihei clucks]
-[Moana shushes]

75
00:03:31,458 --> 00:03:32,542
-[thunder crashes]
-[Moana yelps]

76
00:03:33,208 --> 00:03:34,667
[snakes hissing]

77
00:03:37,458 --> 00:03:39,167
[Kaa] Oh. [chuckles]

78
00:03:39,250 --> 00:03:41,333
Would you like to...

79
00:03:41,417 --> 00:03:44,292
join us? [hisses]

80
00:03:44,375 --> 00:03:47,708
Join you.

81
00:03:48,208 --> 00:03:49,250
[screams]

82
00:03:50,292 --> 00:03:51,417
[gasps] No!

83
00:03:51,500 --> 00:03:53,167
Nope. Nope, nope, nope, nope, nope!

84
00:03:53,250 --> 00:03:54,542
[hissing]

85
00:03:54,625 --> 00:03:56,417
[panting]

86
00:03:56,500 --> 00:03:58,667
Dolphins? In the fountain?

87
00:03:58,750 --> 00:04:00,458
-[Cheshire Cat laughs]
-[dolphins clicking]

88
00:04:01,792 --> 00:04:02,792
[Founder] Help!

89
00:04:02,875 --> 00:04:05,750
Ariel! Help! Ariel!

90
00:04:06,500 --> 00:04:08,208
Flounder! [grunts]

91
00:04:11,750 --> 00:04:13,417
Flounder, where are you?

92
00:04:13,500 --> 00:04:15,542
Whoa, whoa! [yelling] Ariel!

93
00:04:15,625 --> 00:04:16,625
[gasps]

94
00:04:19,125 --> 00:04:20,667
[Flounder panting]

95
00:04:20,750 --> 00:04:21,833
[yells]

96
00:04:23,125 --> 00:04:24,667
[panting]

97
00:04:26,125 --> 00:04:28,833
[grunting]

98
00:04:28,917 --> 00:04:29,917
Uh...

99
00:04:30,000 --> 00:04:31,875
[screaming]

100
00:04:32,625 --> 00:04:34,458
-[screaming continues]
-[Ariel] Come with me!

101
00:04:38,833 --> 00:04:40,167
Oh! Thanks!

102
00:04:41,708 --> 00:04:42,792
[panting]

103
00:04:43,917 --> 00:04:45,792
-[grunts]
-[Flunder yelling]

104
00:04:46,417 --> 00:04:47,417
[growls]

105
00:04:48,500 --> 00:04:49,667
[crunch]

106
00:04:49,750 --> 00:04:50,833
[Ariel chuckles]

107
00:04:53,917 --> 00:04:55,917
-[Flunder screams]
-[Ariel grunts]

108
00:04:56,000 --> 00:04:57,083
Ariel!

109
00:04:57,625 --> 00:04:58,708
[gasps]

110
00:05:02,000 --> 00:05:03,583
[dolphins clicking]

111
00:05:04,125 --> 00:05:07,417
Ugh! [spits, sighs] Thanks!

112
00:05:09,125 --> 00:05:10,708
Hm. Hm.

113
00:05:10,792 --> 00:05:13,167
[Jasmine] [panting] Are they gone?

114
00:05:13,250 --> 00:05:15,458
There aren't any bears behind me,
are there?

115
00:05:15,542 --> 00:05:16,833
-[Jasmine yelps]
-[Moana screams]

116
00:05:16,917 --> 00:05:18,333
-[both screaming]
-[Heihei clucks]

117
00:05:18,417 --> 00:05:19,417
[Mulan] Let me guess.

118
00:05:19,500 --> 00:05:22,500
Did everyone else stumble upon
a bunch of animals in the castle?

119
00:05:22,583 --> 00:05:26,250
The kitchen certainly isn't lacking
any bare necessities.

120
00:05:26,333 --> 00:05:28,000
Was the upstairs clear, Moana?

121
00:05:28,083 --> 00:05:30,375
No, no!
Nope-ity, nope, nope, nope, nope, nope.

122
00:05:30,458 --> 00:05:33,333
Would anyone happen to have
a better Flounder-holder?

123
00:05:33,417 --> 00:05:35,167
[monkeys screeching]

124
00:05:35,250 --> 00:05:39,417
Thank you. Next question.
Has anyone seen Rapunzel?

125
00:05:39,500 --> 00:05:40,583
[Rapunzel screaming]

126
00:05:40,667 --> 00:05:42,833
[screaming continues, grunts]

127
00:05:42,917 --> 00:05:44,583
-Oh, no!
-Ugh!

128
00:05:44,667 --> 00:05:47,292
How did all these animals
get inside the castle?

129
00:05:47,375 --> 00:05:48,833
[coughing]

130
00:05:48,917 --> 00:05:51,292
Every window and door is shut.

131
00:05:51,375 --> 00:05:53,292
Hm. I bet they have the answer.

132
00:05:53,375 --> 00:05:55,500
[Mulan and Jasmine] Hm.

133
00:05:55,583 --> 00:05:57,250
Follow that ant trail!

134
00:05:57,333 --> 00:05:59,333
[Beaver] Eh, let's see here...

135
00:05:59,417 --> 00:06:04,125
[grunting] This is...
heavier than it looks.

136
00:06:04,208 --> 00:06:06,208
You're building a dam indoors?

137
00:06:06,292 --> 00:06:08,250
Well, uh, safety first, sonny!

138
00:06:08,333 --> 00:06:10,750
You never know
when water will come a-rushin'!

139
00:06:10,833 --> 00:06:13,042
Gotta get these logs movin'!

140
00:06:13,125 --> 00:06:16,417
Water indoors?
I didn't even know that could happen.

141
00:06:16,500 --> 00:06:20,750
Finally, someone understands
the importance of indoor damming.

142
00:06:22,042 --> 00:06:24,667
[chuckling] Oh! Now, that's a stick!

143
00:06:25,375 --> 00:06:29,000
[groans] Amelia, if I walk much farther,
I'll get flat feet.

144
00:06:29,083 --> 00:06:32,458
Now, don't you start
with that again, Abigail. [gasps]

145
00:06:32,542 --> 00:06:36,458
Oh. Oh, my. There must be some big event
going on down the hall.

146
00:06:36,542 --> 00:06:39,292
[gasps] Oh, fancy that.
We must get tickets.

147
00:06:39,375 --> 00:06:40,750
Oh, indeed! [chuckles]

148
00:06:40,833 --> 00:06:42,083
[Mulan panting]

149
00:06:42,167 --> 00:06:45,792
The ants are coming from inside this room!
Let's go!

150
00:06:45,875 --> 00:06:47,542
-[animal sounds]
-[Mulan gasps]

151
00:06:51,167 --> 00:06:54,083
Oh, thank goodness! [chuckling]
You're all here!

152
00:06:54,167 --> 00:06:56,125
Animals just keep coming through.

153
00:06:56,208 --> 00:06:58,792
[gasps] I'm exposed!

154
00:06:58,875 --> 00:07:01,833
They are coming into the castle
through Wardrobe's portal!

155
00:07:01,917 --> 00:07:04,667
-Quick! Let's help Wardrobe!
-[chuckling]

156
00:07:06,542 --> 00:07:08,375
[gasps, yells]

157
00:07:09,125 --> 00:07:10,208
Whoa!

158
00:07:11,833 --> 00:07:12,833
[growling]

159
00:07:12,917 --> 00:07:13,917
Uh...

160
00:07:14,000 --> 00:07:15,875
-[monkeys chattering]
-[Rapunzel grunts]

161
00:07:16,833 --> 00:07:17,833
Oh.

162
00:07:19,250 --> 00:07:20,333
[Ariel grunts]

163
00:07:20,417 --> 00:07:21,667
[Flounder groans]

164
00:07:22,208 --> 00:07:23,292
[panting]

165
00:07:24,083 --> 00:07:26,250
[grunts] Whoa!

166
00:07:26,333 --> 00:07:27,792
[bears growling]

167
00:07:27,875 --> 00:07:28,958
[panting]

168
00:07:31,417 --> 00:07:32,500
Nope!

169
00:07:33,917 --> 00:07:35,500
-[Rapunzel grunts]
-[Wardrobe yelps]

170
00:07:37,625 --> 00:07:38,708
[grunts]

171
00:07:39,875 --> 00:07:41,958
Phew! Sure glad that's over.

172
00:07:42,042 --> 00:07:43,917
-That was neat!
-[Moana chuckles]

173
00:07:44,000 --> 00:07:46,083
Now we can get these animals home safely.

174
00:07:46,167 --> 00:07:50,000
And get back to our card game.
I had a winning hand.

175
00:07:50,083 --> 00:07:52,875
Um, Wardrobe, why are you pink?

176
00:07:52,958 --> 00:07:58,000
Whoa. You'd be pink, too, if you had
this many critters in your drawers!

177
00:07:58,083 --> 00:08:00,583
-No, this pink seems...
-[Cheshire Cat chuckles]

178
00:08:00,667 --> 00:08:01,917
Enchanted.

179
00:08:03,167 --> 00:08:05,250
Oh, dear, that can't be good.

180
00:08:05,333 --> 00:08:07,500
[gasps] Oh! Whoa!

181
00:08:07,583 --> 00:08:09,042
-[neighing]
-[monkeys chattering]

182
00:08:09,125 --> 00:08:10,542
[growling]

183
00:08:11,333 --> 00:08:13,167
Where are the animals going?

184
00:08:13,250 --> 00:08:16,375
I mean, animals always flee
when they sense danger.

185
00:08:16,458 --> 00:08:19,042
-[rumbling]
-Look out, everyone!

186
00:08:19,125 --> 00:08:21,833
-This armoire's gonna blow!
-[elephants trumpeting]

187
00:08:21,917 --> 00:08:23,458
Oh, dear!

188
00:08:23,542 --> 00:08:25,167
[grunts]

189
00:08:25,250 --> 00:08:26,750
Stampede!

190
00:08:26,833 --> 00:08:28,333
[trumpeting]

191
00:08:30,167 --> 00:08:31,250
[grunts]

192
00:08:31,333 --> 00:08:33,375
Uh, Ariel? [grunts]

193
00:08:33,458 --> 00:08:36,542
-May I?
-Of course! Thanks for asking.

194
00:08:37,333 --> 00:08:39,625
I'll always save your tail.

195
00:08:39,708 --> 00:08:41,792
-[elephants trumpeting]
-[Mulan panting]

196
00:08:41,875 --> 00:08:43,042
[grunts]

197
00:08:43,125 --> 00:08:44,875
Heads up, Moana!

198
00:08:45,542 --> 00:08:47,083
[grunting]

199
00:08:48,542 --> 00:08:49,625
[yelps]

200
00:08:49,708 --> 00:08:51,458
[grunts] Let's lead them outside!

201
00:08:52,167 --> 00:08:53,333
[trumpeting]

202
00:08:53,417 --> 00:08:55,208
How do you steer these things?

203
00:09:00,375 --> 00:09:02,375
[elephants trumpeting]

204
00:09:04,500 --> 00:09:05,833
[Mulan] Hold on, everyone!

205
00:09:09,250 --> 00:09:10,917
This way. Huh?

206
00:09:13,875 --> 00:09:16,792
Huh. Oh, no, we're not going to fit!

207
00:09:16,875 --> 00:09:18,458
-[animal sounds]
-[Amelia] Oh, dear.

208
00:09:18,542 --> 00:09:21,292
It must be intermission!
Well, that was rather quick!

209
00:09:21,375 --> 00:09:26,000
Oh, excuse me, madam.
May I ask how you're enjoying the show?

210
00:09:26,083 --> 00:09:27,292
[elephants trumpeting]

211
00:09:27,375 --> 00:09:29,125
My dam!

212
00:09:29,208 --> 00:09:32,167
Ah, I didn't account for pachyderms!
[grunts]

213
00:09:32,250 --> 00:09:33,250
[crashing]

214
00:09:33,333 --> 00:09:35,792
[animal sounds]

215
00:09:40,208 --> 00:09:43,875
[groans] This was supposed to be
a relaxing day!

216
00:09:44,500 --> 00:09:46,583
This is not the face of a person relaxed!

217
00:09:46,667 --> 00:09:49,542
It could be worse!
At least we're still warm and dry.

218
00:09:49,625 --> 00:09:50,625
[thunder crashes]

219
00:09:50,708 --> 00:09:53,458
Um, why was that rumble so ominous?

220
00:09:53,958 --> 00:09:56,000
Something's headed our way.

221
00:09:56,833 --> 00:09:58,750
[Beaver] No! It can't be.

222
00:10:02,708 --> 00:10:03,792
Water!

223
00:10:07,917 --> 00:10:09,792
Gotta rebuild the dam!

224
00:10:12,000 --> 00:10:14,333
Hurray! That was close.

225
00:10:14,417 --> 00:10:16,833
[yells, groans]

226
00:10:16,917 --> 00:10:18,458
You better put these on.

227
00:10:20,542 --> 00:10:22,000
[Beaver] Gosh darn it!

228
00:10:26,500 --> 00:10:28,833
-[all screaming]
-No, no! No, no, no!

229
00:10:28,917 --> 00:10:30,000
[Beaver cries]

230
00:10:33,292 --> 00:10:37,250
[sighs] Who needs a bathtub
when there's an indoor swimming pool?

231
00:10:37,333 --> 00:10:40,875
Truer words were never spoken, sister.
[chuckles]

232
00:10:40,958 --> 00:10:43,500
I give these lodgings five stars!

233
00:10:43,583 --> 00:10:47,000
Four, sister.
Housekeeping is not up to snuff.

234
00:10:47,083 --> 00:10:48,417
-Really?
-Mm-hmm.

235
00:10:48,500 --> 00:10:49,583
[laughs]

236
00:10:52,083 --> 00:10:55,417
[sighs] So this is what it's like
to live under the sea.

237
00:10:55,500 --> 00:10:57,083
I thought there'd be more dancing.

238
00:10:57,167 --> 00:11:00,292
Um, it's not always better down
where it's wetter.

239
00:11:00,375 --> 00:11:02,125
-Common misconception.
-[thunder crashes]

240
00:11:02,208 --> 00:11:03,208
[both gasp]

241
00:11:03,292 --> 00:11:04,917
[laughing]

242
00:11:08,833 --> 00:11:12,458
Have you noticed that every time
thunder claps, something bad happens?

243
00:11:12,542 --> 00:11:14,625
It can't get any worse than this!

244
00:11:20,375 --> 00:11:21,833
[coughing]

245
00:11:21,917 --> 00:11:23,792
I don't wanna jinx it...

246
00:11:24,625 --> 00:11:25,875
Then please don't.

247
00:11:25,958 --> 00:11:28,000
But that's got to be it, right?

248
00:11:28,083 --> 00:11:29,875
Don't say it, Rapunzel.

249
00:11:29,958 --> 00:11:32,583
-I mean, what else could go wrong?
-[Pascal trills]

250
00:11:32,667 --> 00:11:35,083
-[thunder crashes]
-I wouldn't ask that out loud.

251
00:11:39,917 --> 00:11:41,208
[squealing]

252
00:11:47,917 --> 00:11:49,667
[Rapunzel] Oh, no.

253
00:11:50,375 --> 00:11:51,875
[Cheshire Cat laughing]

254
00:11:57,417 --> 00:11:58,542
[Magic Mirror mumbles]

255
00:12:03,458 --> 00:12:04,875
[Rapunzel] What are those things?

256
00:12:04,958 --> 00:12:07,792
Runaway foliage!

257
00:12:09,208 --> 00:12:11,167
[Rapunzel] We have to save the animals!

258
00:12:11,250 --> 00:12:12,417
[grunting]

259
00:12:12,500 --> 00:12:13,792
[yelps]

260
00:12:14,417 --> 00:12:15,458
[grunts]

261
00:12:15,958 --> 00:12:18,042
Pua! [grunts]

262
00:12:18,125 --> 00:12:19,208
I got you.

263
00:12:19,292 --> 00:12:20,375
[yelps]

264
00:12:20,458 --> 00:12:22,875
[grunting]

265
00:12:25,375 --> 00:12:26,375
Close the windows!

266
00:12:26,958 --> 00:12:28,625
-[grunts] Come on, Raj-- [screams]
-[Rajah growls]

267
00:12:31,292 --> 00:12:32,750
Let's get you out of here.

268
00:12:33,458 --> 00:12:34,542
[Rapunzel grunts]

269
00:12:39,125 --> 00:12:40,208
[yells]

270
00:12:40,292 --> 00:12:41,917
[screams]

271
00:12:42,333 --> 00:12:43,667
[grunts]

272
00:12:43,750 --> 00:12:46,792
I have no idea
how I'm brushing this mess out.

273
00:12:46,875 --> 00:12:48,458
Thanks a lot, vines.

274
00:12:48,542 --> 00:12:50,792
Oh, now this is a show. [laughs]

275
00:12:50,875 --> 00:12:52,667
I'm so glad we caught the second half!
[laughs]

276
00:12:52,750 --> 00:12:54,833
Yes, the drama! [chuckles]

277
00:12:54,917 --> 00:12:57,000
[grunts] What do we do?

278
00:12:57,083 --> 00:12:58,958
We need a sword!

279
00:12:59,042 --> 00:13:00,458
Or a machete!

280
00:13:01,000 --> 00:13:05,000
Or, oh! An axe!
Magic Mirror, can you help us?

281
00:13:05,083 --> 00:13:07,167
[blowing] Yeah.

282
00:13:07,250 --> 00:13:11,125
Skilled with tools is one you seek...

283
00:13:11,208 --> 00:13:12,708
-[Magic Mirror speaks indistinctly]
-Magic Mirror?

284
00:13:12,792 --> 00:13:16,792
I'm afraid there simply is no time
for dulcet tones or a poetic rhyme.

285
00:13:16,875 --> 00:13:19,250
[Ariel] We need the Princess
here right quick,

286
00:13:19,333 --> 00:13:21,625
-before the vines become too thick!
-[Heihei yelps]

287
00:13:22,333 --> 00:13:23,958
Very well.

288
00:13:24,042 --> 00:13:25,875
[disembodied voice breathing deeply]

289
00:13:28,542 --> 00:13:32,458
Did someone call for an axe?

290
00:13:32,542 --> 00:13:33,625
[laughing]

291
00:13:33,708 --> 00:13:35,417
-Snow White!
-I knew you'd make it!

292
00:13:35,500 --> 00:13:37,625
[giggles] Oh!

293
00:13:38,375 --> 00:13:39,458
Huh?

294
00:13:39,542 --> 00:13:40,542
Oh!

295
00:13:40,625 --> 00:13:41,958
[Snow White] How did you get in there?

296
00:13:42,042 --> 00:13:43,958
Well, it's off to work I go!

297
00:13:45,208 --> 00:13:46,292
[grunts, chuckles]

298
00:13:51,542 --> 00:13:52,625
[chuckles]

299
00:13:53,542 --> 00:13:54,625
[growls]

300
00:14:02,958 --> 00:14:04,042
[Heihei squawks]

301
00:14:04,125 --> 00:14:05,167
[yells]

302
00:14:07,542 --> 00:14:08,917
[Snow White chuckles, grunts]

303
00:14:09,417 --> 00:14:10,500
[thumping]

304
00:14:12,500 --> 00:14:14,500
[grunting]

305
00:14:15,583 --> 00:14:17,167
[chuckling]

306
00:14:17,250 --> 00:14:18,458
[straining]

307
00:14:21,417 --> 00:14:22,500
[grunting]

308
00:14:24,542 --> 00:14:26,208
[screaming]

309
00:14:26,708 --> 00:14:27,792
No!

310
00:14:28,792 --> 00:14:31,292
-No!
-Got caught up in the moment. [chuckles]

311
00:14:35,625 --> 00:14:37,833
-So much hair.
-So much hair.

312
00:14:37,917 --> 00:14:41,000
Yes, I get it. I have a lot of hair.

313
00:14:41,083 --> 00:14:42,708
Mm. Done.

314
00:14:43,458 --> 00:14:44,458
-Yes!
-[sighs]

315
00:14:45,000 --> 00:14:47,250
Where did this land seaweed come from?

316
00:14:47,333 --> 00:14:48,417
[bird chirping]

317
00:14:53,333 --> 00:14:55,792
This must have been some party.

318
00:14:55,875 --> 00:14:59,750
We were having a quiet, rainy day indoors.
Then all of a sudden...

319
00:14:59,833 --> 00:15:02,292
Bunnies. [grunts] Everywhere.

320
00:15:02,375 --> 00:15:04,583
-Everywhere.
-How lucky!

321
00:15:04,667 --> 00:15:07,667
And other creatures, too,
all coming in through the portals.

322
00:15:07,750 --> 00:15:10,083
[sighs] But we're not sure why.

323
00:15:10,167 --> 00:15:13,875
That's strange.
Let me ask our friend what she knows.

324
00:15:14,500 --> 00:15:18,250
Mm-hmm. Mm-hmm. Mm-hmm!

325
00:15:18,333 --> 00:15:20,750
Oh! She says she was invited.

326
00:15:21,292 --> 00:15:23,292
-Invited?
-[thunder crashes]

327
00:15:24,167 --> 00:15:25,667
[creaking]

328
00:15:28,750 --> 00:15:30,917
The castle's going to collapse!

329
00:15:31,500 --> 00:15:33,917
[grunts] We have to get the animals
out of here.

330
00:15:34,000 --> 00:15:35,583
Before the ceiling caves in!

331
00:15:35,667 --> 00:15:37,792
-But how?
-There's too many of them

332
00:15:37,875 --> 00:15:39,167
and not enough of us!

333
00:15:39,250 --> 00:15:41,500
[Mushu] Did I hear someone
ask for a miracle?

334
00:15:41,583 --> 00:15:43,542
Let me hear ya say... [yelling] Ah!

335
00:15:43,625 --> 00:15:44,917
[yelling] Ah!

336
00:15:45,000 --> 00:15:46,417
That's close enough!

337
00:15:46,500 --> 00:15:47,667
[gasps] Mushu!

338
00:15:47,750 --> 00:15:48,792
[all chuckling]

339
00:15:51,542 --> 00:15:53,417
-[laughter]
-Hurray!

340
00:15:54,000 --> 00:15:55,458
I'm so glad to see you.

341
00:15:55,542 --> 00:15:58,833
[chuckles] You know I'm always ready
to jump in and help you,

342
00:15:58,917 --> 00:16:01,667
but we are gonna talk later
about you not invitin' me to this party,

343
00:16:01,750 --> 00:16:04,125
'cause this looked epic!

344
00:16:04,208 --> 00:16:05,542
[thunder crashes]

345
00:16:05,625 --> 00:16:08,042
Hurry! Before we're all royal rubble!

346
00:16:08,125 --> 00:16:10,292
Now let's make this cinematic!

347
00:16:13,625 --> 00:16:15,625
-[narrator] Mushu!
-[laughing]

348
00:16:17,542 --> 00:16:18,625
[screaming]

349
00:16:19,542 --> 00:16:20,667
[Mushu chuckles]

350
00:16:20,750 --> 00:16:22,458
All right, move it along!
Little guys in front.

351
00:16:22,542 --> 00:16:24,958
[animal sounds]

352
00:16:25,042 --> 00:16:27,208
Careful now. Don't trample the dragon.

353
00:16:30,250 --> 00:16:31,750
[animal sounds]

354
00:16:33,167 --> 00:16:34,708
[monkeys screeching]

355
00:16:35,167 --> 00:16:36,167
[whistles]

356
00:16:38,625 --> 00:16:39,750
[narrator] Carpet!

357
00:16:43,292 --> 00:16:44,375
Rajah!

358
00:16:46,917 --> 00:16:48,000
[Rajah roars]

359
00:16:48,500 --> 00:16:50,083
[monkeys screeching]

360
00:16:54,917 --> 00:16:57,042
Um, anyone down here?

361
00:16:57,125 --> 00:16:58,208
[Pascal trills]

362
00:17:00,833 --> 00:17:02,500
-[squeals]
-[narrator] Pascal!

363
00:17:02,583 --> 00:17:03,667
[Pascal trilling]

364
00:17:07,042 --> 00:17:08,958
[Rapunzel screaming]

365
00:17:09,458 --> 00:17:10,708
Everybody out!

366
00:17:10,792 --> 00:17:11,958
[clucks]

367
00:17:15,542 --> 00:17:16,875
[narrator] Heihei!

368
00:17:16,958 --> 00:17:18,167
[caws]

369
00:17:19,750 --> 00:17:20,833
Pua!

370
00:17:22,042 --> 00:17:23,250
[grunts, yells]

371
00:17:24,792 --> 00:17:25,875
[growls]

372
00:17:26,375 --> 00:17:28,125
-[Heihei caws]
-Nice bears?

373
00:17:28,208 --> 00:17:30,917
-[Moana screaming]
-[Heihei clucking]

374
00:17:31,000 --> 00:17:33,167
Not a great hair day!

375
00:17:33,917 --> 00:17:35,917
[snakes hissing]

376
00:17:38,167 --> 00:17:39,250
[narrator] Flounder!

377
00:17:39,333 --> 00:17:40,417
[blows raspberry]

378
00:17:41,458 --> 00:17:43,625
-[snakes hissing]
-Uh... Uh...

379
00:17:43,708 --> 00:17:45,292
You can't get me! [laughs]

380
00:17:50,125 --> 00:17:51,208
[Flunder laughing]

381
00:17:57,042 --> 00:17:58,125
Wait.

382
00:17:58,208 --> 00:17:59,458
Where's Snow White?

383
00:18:00,875 --> 00:18:02,292
There's no time to lose.

384
00:18:02,375 --> 00:18:03,708
You have to leave immediately!

385
00:18:04,375 --> 00:18:05,792
Oh! Whoa!

386
00:18:07,792 --> 00:18:09,792
[screaming]

387
00:18:12,958 --> 00:18:14,125
[screaming continues]

388
00:18:15,292 --> 00:18:17,417
-[grunts]
-[birds chirping]

389
00:18:17,500 --> 00:18:19,375
Oh. How nice.

390
00:18:23,000 --> 00:18:25,000
-[chuckles, gasps]
-[rumbling]

391
00:18:25,083 --> 00:18:26,917
[rumbling]

392
00:18:29,708 --> 00:18:30,792
[crashing]

393
00:18:34,167 --> 00:18:35,958
Oh, goodness.

394
00:18:36,042 --> 00:18:37,458
I can't believe it.

395
00:18:40,708 --> 00:18:42,458
That's a lot of bricks.

396
00:18:46,542 --> 00:18:47,625
[thud]

397
00:18:50,375 --> 00:18:53,000
[sighs] Such a splendid holiday, Amelia.
[chuckles]

398
00:18:53,083 --> 00:18:54,167
Oh, quite, Abigail.

399
00:18:54,250 --> 00:18:57,750
Though a little more crowded
than I had expected for such a big castle.

400
00:18:57,833 --> 00:18:59,083
-[Heihei caws]
-Oh!

401
00:18:59,167 --> 00:19:00,250
Oh, dear.

402
00:19:00,333 --> 00:19:01,542
Do you think we should come back?

403
00:19:01,625 --> 00:19:02,708
-[Heihei clucks]
-[Amelia] Why not?

404
00:19:02,792 --> 00:19:05,292
I do so love an exciting holiday.

405
00:19:08,583 --> 00:19:10,583
[animal sounds]

406
00:19:14,542 --> 00:19:15,625
[Rajah growls]

407
00:19:17,458 --> 00:19:20,167
[grunts, gasps] Oh, oh!
[chuckles nervously]

408
00:19:21,750 --> 00:19:22,750
[Mulan] Well...

409
00:19:23,250 --> 00:19:26,875
Building with bricks is one of my favorite
rainy-day activities.

410
00:19:26,958 --> 00:19:28,667
But why did this happen?

411
00:19:28,750 --> 00:19:33,000
And why was there always a flash of pink
with every shift?

412
00:19:33,083 --> 00:19:35,167
A flash of pink, you say?

413
00:19:35,250 --> 00:19:39,042
Only one creature
could pull off a day like today, and...

414
00:19:39,125 --> 00:19:40,167
[caws]

415
00:19:40,250 --> 00:19:42,250
...punctuate it with that color.

416
00:19:42,333 --> 00:19:44,042
[yelling] Cheshire Cat!

417
00:19:44,125 --> 00:19:48,042
Ta-da! [chuckles] That's me.

418
00:19:48,125 --> 00:19:50,875
-Are you hurt?
-A frayed whisker.

419
00:19:50,958 --> 00:19:54,208
Nothing a little tea won't fix.

420
00:19:54,292 --> 00:19:56,833
While you finish your tea,
maybe you can tell us

421
00:19:56,917 --> 00:19:59,667
why you brought all these animals
into the castle?

422
00:19:59,750 --> 00:20:02,333
-And the water?
-And the vines?

423
00:20:02,417 --> 00:20:03,667
That was a bit much.

424
00:20:03,750 --> 00:20:07,625
Now, now.
It was just a bit of rainy-day fun!

425
00:20:07,708 --> 00:20:11,042
Rainy-day fun
doesn't destroy an entire castle.

426
00:20:11,125 --> 00:20:15,417
Tell me, are you all mad?

427
00:20:15,500 --> 00:20:16,583
Mad?

428
00:20:17,083 --> 00:20:19,292
Steaming mad?

429
00:20:19,375 --> 00:20:21,500
No, Cheshire Cat, we aren't mad.

430
00:20:21,833 --> 00:20:24,542
Uh, actually...
[chuckles] I am a little mad.

431
00:20:24,625 --> 00:20:26,708
But we are ready to rebuild.

432
00:20:26,792 --> 00:20:29,375
And you're going to help us!

433
00:20:29,458 --> 00:20:31,667
-[sighs]
-Would you like me to whistle?

434
00:20:31,750 --> 00:20:32,750
While you work?

435
00:20:32,833 --> 00:20:35,958
That won't be necessary.

436
00:20:38,708 --> 00:20:40,042
[thunder crashes]

437
00:20:40,833 --> 00:20:41,833
[laughing]

438
00:20:45,375 --> 00:20:47,375
[clattering]

439
00:20:50,125 --> 00:20:52,125
[vocalizing]

440
00:20:57,125 --> 00:20:58,500
[chuckling]

441
00:20:58,958 --> 00:21:00,500
[vocalizing]

442
00:21:01,000 --> 00:21:02,667
[Wardrobe] Oh, for heaven's sake!

443
00:21:05,292 --> 00:21:06,958
Would you look at that!

444
00:21:07,042 --> 00:21:08,875
[Ariel] [chuckling]
It's even better than before!

445
00:21:09,250 --> 00:21:11,375
[gasps] Come on, everyone!
Let's go check it out!

446
00:21:11,458 --> 00:21:13,208
-[Jasmine] Yes!
-[Rapunzel] Amazing!

447
00:21:13,292 --> 00:21:15,792
My work here is done. [sighs]

448
00:21:15,875 --> 00:21:17,583
Now I'm bored.

449
00:21:17,667 --> 00:21:19,833
Where to... [chuckling] next?

450
00:21:19,917 --> 00:21:22,917
[princesses cheering and laughing]

451
00:21:23,000 --> 00:21:25,292
[Jasmine] It's all so magical!

452
00:21:25,375 --> 00:21:26,500
[Mulan] Oh, I love it.

453
00:21:26,583 --> 00:21:29,792
-[Snow White] [gasps] How wonderful!
-[Moana] [chuckling] All right!

454
00:21:29,875 --> 00:21:31,875
[Ariel] Oh, have you seen anything

455
00:21:31,958 --> 00:21:34,792
so wonderful in your entire life?

456
00:21:34,875 --> 00:21:37,583
[Rapunzel]
Nothing could possibly go wrong now.

457
00:21:37,667 --> 00:21:39,333
[all] Rapunzel!

458
00:21:41,125 --> 00:21:43,125
[theme music playing]